    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 273 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented city title-casing on owner creation with reuse of existing spellings.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `NormalizeCity.java` (`rest/function/owner/`): given the newly built owner, it scans existing owners for one whose city matches case-insensitively. If found, it reuses that owner's exact city spelling; otherwise it title-cases the city (each whitespace-separated word capitalized, remainder lower-cased).\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 inserted a `normalizeCity` step into `owners.POST.yml` between `checkDuplicate` and `assignMembershipNumber`, under the same `transaction` governance. It runs before `save`, so the \"already exists\" check reflects only pre-existing owners.\n\nBoth new Cp12 tests (`coreTitleCasesCity`, `functionalityReusesExistingCitySpelling`) and the full suite (273 tests) are green.",
